//
// Mohio Sector Profile -- Demo Financial  (SAMPLE / non-certified, public)
// sector: demo_financial
//
// PURPOSE: exercise sector-tightens-a-compliance-profile layering end to end, using SOC 2 as the
// floor. Named `demo_financial` rather than the bare `financial` name deliberately -- `financial`
// is a reserved, paid-tier sector name (`mohio_sector_loader.PAID_SECTORS`) whose real profile is
// commercial and never ships in the open build; this is a public test fixture, not a real
// financial-sector artifact, and it does not claim to be one.
//
// THIS IS NOT A COMPLIANCE CONTROL. Not legally reviewed, no certified standing. The framework
// names below activate the grade mapping in `mohio_audit_grades.py`; they are not a ruling on
// what SOX/SOC 2 actually require of any real organization.
//
// THE LAYERING THIS FILE DEMONSTRATES (composition mechanism, verified live 2026-09-04):
// Mohio has no "sector includes another profile file" primitive -- there is no import/reference
// syntax that pulls in `sector-demo-soc2.sector` by name. Composition today is DECLARATIVE and
// ADDITIVE: a sector's own `compliance:` lines are just more framework names appended to the same
// list a program's own `compliance:` declarations feed (see `mohio_interpreter._exec_ComplianceDecl`,
// P0-2 2026-09-02 fix). `required_grade()` then takes the HIGHEST grade across the whole list.
// So this file "calls and tightens" the SOC 2 floor the only way the mechanism supports today:
// by declaring `soc2` (the floor) AND `sox` (a stricter framework, mapped to `worm`) side by
// side. The composed result is `worm`, never lower than either framework alone would require --
// which matches the RULED model's "a sector never lowers a protection, it only adds" even though
// there is no dedicated "call another profile" primitive to enforce that structurally. That gap
// -- no file-level composition/inheritance between profiles -- is a real, named finding of this
// probe, not fixed here.
//
// VERIFIED RESULT: a program under `sector: demo_financial`, writing to a real (file-backed,
// `durable`-grade) SQLite sink, is NOT sufficient -- `durable` does not satisfy the `worm` floor
// this file raises the requirement to, so the write is durably recorded but flagged as a
// DEGRADED audit incident pending reconciliation to grade, exactly the outcome the ladder in
// `mohio_audit_grades.py` describes. The SAME sink, under `sector: demo_soc2` alone (floor
// `durable`), satisfies the requirement cleanly with no incident. This is the live evidence that
// the sector's addition of `sox` genuinely raised the floor beyond what SOC 2 alone required --
// see the probe report for the exact commands and output.

sector: demo_financial
    meta
        version "0.1"
        maintainer "Mohio community sample"
        tier "community"
        note "Demo profile: SOC 2 floor tightened to WORM. Not legally reviewed. No certified compliance."
    meta: done

    // The floor this sector builds on.
    compliance: soc2
    // The tightening: sox maps to "worm" in FRAMEWORK_AUDIT_GRADE, raising the composed
    // requirement above soc2's own "durable" floor. Never removes soc2's requirement, only adds
    // a stricter one on top -- composition is additive, per `required_grade()`'s max-across-list
    // rule.
    compliance: sox

    // A retention rule, layered the same additive way: financial recordkeeping regimes (SOX,
    // SEC 17a-4) require years-long retention of records touching payment/financial data, well
    // beyond anything SOC 2 itself mandates.
    retain all [pci] for 7 years

    // ── WHAT THE ENFORCEMENT MECHANISM NEEDS SOMETHING TO FIRE ON (added 2026-09-14) ──
    //
    // Until now this profile declared frameworks and a retention rule and nothing else, which
    // exercised the audit-grade ladder and left three of the flagship controls with nothing to
    // act on: no field carried a classification, no field was refused at compile time, and no
    // decision had a floor to clear. So `sector: demo_financial` demonstrated part of the
    // mechanism and reported the rest as inactive, which reads as the controls not existing.
    //
    // STILL NOT A COMPLIANCE CONTROL. These are the smallest rules that make each control
    // OBSERVABLE, chosen to look like a financial program rather than to be a ruling on what
    // any regime requires of anybody.

    field types
        // REFUSED AT COMPILE TIME, which is the strongest of these: a shape declaring one of
        // these fields produces no build at all, so the violation never reaches a running
        // system and there is nothing to clean up afterwards.
        card_number is [pci]
            never store
            label "Payment card number"
        account_number is [pci, pii]
            never store
            label "Bank account number"
        // CLASSIFIED BUT STORABLE, which is the other half. A field can be governed without
        // being forbidden, and a profile that only ever refuses cannot show the difference.
        member_id is [pii]
            label "Member identifier"
        amount is [financial]
            label "Transaction amount"
    field: done

    // THE FLOOR AN AI DECISION MUST CLEAR. Without one declared, a decision under this sector
    // had nothing to be measured against and the governance check had nothing to report.
    ai.decide rules for sector "demo_financial"
        minimum confidence 0.85 for transaction_decision
        minimum confidence 0.95 for account_closure
    ai.decide: done
